1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,457
The Curiosity Club.

2
00:00:02,457 --> 00:00:04,517
Episode 3.

3
00:00:04,517 --> 00:00:07,187
The Paper Bridge Challenge.

4
00:00:07,187 --> 00:00:10,028
Here is something to listen for.

5
00:00:10,028 --> 00:00:13,849
What did Maya change in the first improved bridge?

6
00:00:13,849 --> 00:00:15,340
Ready?

7
00:00:15,340 --> 00:00:17,514
Let us find out.

8
00:00:17,514 --> 00:00:20,497
The science club has a challenge.

9
00:00:20,497 --> 00:00:24,957
Build a bridge between two books using one sheet of paper.

10
00:00:24,957 --> 00:00:28,437
Then see how many small blocks it can hold.

11
00:00:28,437 --> 00:00:31,335
Leo lays his paper flat.

12
00:00:31,335 --> 00:00:35,113
This is a very fast bridge, he says.

13
00:00:35,113 --> 00:00:37,840
The first block stays on it.

14
00:00:37,840 --> 00:00:41,107
The second block makes the middle bend.

15
00:00:41,107 --> 00:00:45,383
The third block falls through, taking the bridge with it.

16
00:00:45,383 --> 00:00:49,843
Fast to build, Maya says, and fast to fall.

17
00:00:49,843 --> 00:00:52,670
Pip offers to hold the paper up.

18
00:00:52,670 --> 00:00:55,014
Ms. Park smiles.

19
00:00:55,014 --> 00:00:58,920
The bridge has to work without a robot underneath it.

20
00:00:58,920 --> 00:01:03,508
Maya folds her paper back and forth, like a small fan.

21
00:01:03,508 --> 00:01:06,420
She puts it across the same gap.

22
00:01:06,420 --> 00:01:09,772
It holds more blocks before it bends.

23
00:01:09,772 --> 00:01:12,173
Did you use thicker paper?

24
00:01:12,173 --> 00:01:14,204
Leo asks.

25
00:01:14,204 --> 00:01:15,752
No.

26
00:01:15,752 --> 00:01:18,267
We used the same kind.

27
00:01:18,267 --> 00:01:20,539
I changed the shape.

28
00:01:20,539 --> 00:01:26,278
Leo wants to make the gap smaller, add tape, and use two sheets at once.

29
00:01:26,278 --> 00:01:30,056
Let us change one thing first, says Maya.

30
00:01:30,056 --> 00:01:33,025
Then we can understand what helped.

31
00:01:33,025 --> 00:01:37,187
They fold a new sheet and test it over the original gap.

32
00:01:37,187 --> 00:01:40,482
This time, they write down the result.

33
00:01:40,482 --> 00:01:44,588
They also put the blocks in the same place each time.

34
00:01:44,588 --> 00:01:48,082
Pip names the bridge The Great Paper Highway.

35
00:01:48,082 --> 00:01:50,340
Can a bus cross it?

36
00:01:50,340 --> 00:01:52,244
he asks.

37
00:01:52,244 --> 00:01:55,965
A toy bus, perhaps, says Leo.

38
00:01:55,965 --> 00:01:59,772
Pip makes a sign: Small vehicles only.

39
00:01:59,772 --> 00:02:02,727
Large robots must go around.

40
00:02:02,727 --> 00:02:05,767
Now, a little more to discover.

41
00:02:05,767 --> 00:02:09,971
An object's shape can affect how it bends under a load.

42
00:02:09,971 --> 00:02:14,531
Folding paper can make it harder to bend in some directions.

43
00:02:14,531 --> 00:02:19,204
Engineers compare designs, test them, and improve them.

44
00:02:19,204 --> 00:02:25,284
When you change one feature at a time, it is easier to understand why a result changed.

45
00:02:25,284 --> 00:02:28,252
Let us hear the main idea again.

46
00:02:28,252 --> 00:02:31,463
A flat paper bridge bent quickly.

47
00:02:31,463 --> 00:02:35,795
Maya folded the paper and tested it across the same gap.

48
00:02:35,795 --> 00:02:39,488
The new shape held more blocks in their test.

49
00:02:39,488 --> 00:02:44,119
The club learned to compare designs carefully and keep a record.

50
00:02:44,119 --> 00:02:47,230
Here are three useful expressions.

51
00:02:47,230 --> 00:02:50,497
You can listen, or say them with me.

52
00:02:50,497 --> 00:02:52,727
Let us try again.

53
00:02:52,727 --> 00:02:54,957
Let us try again.

54
00:02:54,957 --> 00:02:57,187
What did you change?

55
00:02:57,187 --> 00:02:59,417
What did you change?

56
00:02:59,417 --> 00:03:02,329
We used the same kind of paper.

57
00:03:02,329 --> 00:03:05,241
We used the same kind of paper.

58
00:03:05,241 --> 00:03:07,954
Remember our listening question?

59
00:03:07,954 --> 00:03:11,775
What did Maya change in the first improved bridge?

60
00:03:11,775 --> 00:03:14,005
Here is the answer.

61
00:03:14,005 --> 00:03:17,471
She changed the shape by folding the paper.

62
00:03:17,471 --> 00:03:20,326
She did not use a thicker sheet.

63
00:03:20,326 --> 00:03:24,147
And here is a question just for your imagination.

64
00:03:24,147 --> 00:03:29,914
Where can you see folds, curves, or triangles in things that need to be strong?

65
00:03:29,914 --> 00:03:33,167
There is more than one possible answer.

66
00:03:33,167 --> 00:03:36,562
Keep wondering, and see you next time.
